  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- Mayer seemed to reach another level of playing this music [7]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **China Cat**: back after 48 archived shows (903 days); rare: 5 archived performances [8]\n- **Foolish Heart**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 4 archived performances [8]\n- **Hey Jude**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 13 archived performances [8]\n- **Slipknow**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [8]\n- **Milestones**: rare: 14 archived performances [8]\n- **Watchtower**: back after 184 archived shows (2189 days); rare: 3 archived performances [8]\n- **Going Down The Road**: back after 167 archived shows (2163 days); rare: 5 archived performances [8]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadco2022-06-18** (recommended): source not stated; 21 songs; 181 min; rated 5/5 by 3 [1]\n- **dc2022-06-18**: source not stated; 21 songs; 182 min [2]\n- **deadco2022-06-18.deadco2022-06-18**: source not stated; 21 songs; 181 min [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Folsom is one of the few remaining venues with general admission on the floor, recalling older days [7]\n- Reviewer considers this probably the best Dead and Co show they have heard [5]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadco2022-06-18**: taped by Jeff Travitz [1]\n- **dc2022-06-18**: Recorded with a Soundfield ST-450 cardioid mic into a Sonosax SX-R4 at 24-bit/48k; Transfer from the Sonosax went to Audacity at 16/44, then CD Wave, then FLAC [2]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Poster by Boulder: [2022 Dead and Company poster Boulder Folsom Fueld 6/18/22 | #4477328338](https://www.worthpoint.com/worthopedia/2022-dead-company-poster-boulder-4477328338) [9]",
